<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lihula</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lihula is a small town in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, in Lääne County. In the early 13th century its stronghold was the centre of the Estonian land of Läänemaa, and in 1220 Oeselian islanders destroyed a Swedish garrison there. It then became the first seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Ösel-Wiek, who built a castle there before moving their residence to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haapsalu">Haapsalu</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lihula.jpg" alt="Lihula" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kristian Pikner · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lihula112.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
